textT -- forms step 5, text (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 582). Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh, registered on trunk before the
build: each pinned at today's value with the intended beside it.

firstLight is drawn into its bitmap by drawWalk, and every scan reads that bitmap through the top field. Coordinates are
page coordinates (the top's x and y are the origin). The text inset is 4 points, so a field's first baseline sits at its
top + 4 + the font's ascent: words (Palatino 14, ascent 11.52, line 15.40) at 45.52, 60.92, 76.32; heading (Palatino 24
bold, ascent 19.75) at 23.75; ok at 180.52. SEQ 583 made heading 43 tall, so words starts 13 lower: its baselines are
58.52, 73.92, 89.32 and its scans moved down 13 (TX-2, TX-3, TX-4, TX-5). Metrics measured with Core Text, 2026-11-09.

tForm is this fixture's own form, drawn with explicit frames (no setFrame). tForm names color:=red and font:=normalFont,
so its children inherit both unless they name their own: tOver names blue, tLong inherits red, tStyled takes green and
titleFont from its style tsStyle. tOver is 120 x 40: two lines fit (baselines 25.52, 40.92) and a third (56.32) does not,
so the band y 46..49 holds nothing if the third line is not drawn, and catches its ascenders if it is drawn and clipped.
tPlain (SEQ 583) names no color and no font, nor does its top tPlainTop: black, Helvetica 12. It is a CHILD on
purpose: a top keeps its drawing context in the slot its own text would use, so a top's text is not drawable (textTopT).
tLong's one word is wider than its 60-point frame: it runs to the frame's edge (x 66..69 inked) and stops there (x 70..79
reads tForm's white).

The scans are read by coordinate in formsPop (the first read of each point), so their order does not matter there.
TX-5, the orientation row, reads TX-4's first band: the T of This, top rows y 49..51 against bottom rows y 55..57, x 3..12.
